window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>In the brutal winter of 900 CE, Sigrid, a fierce shieldmaiden of the Frostfang clan, leads a raid on a Northumbrian monastery, capturing Eadric, a young monk whose quiet resilience challenges her world. As a merciless blizzard traps their clan in the icy fjords, an forbidden love ignites between them, defying the gods and traditions that bind their people. Their bond sparks a daring rebellion against the clan’s blood-soaked ways, pitting Sigrid against her rival, Astrid, and the rigid rule of Jarl Hrothgar. With a rival clan’s warband closing in, Sigrid and Eadric must unite a divided people, blending Norse honor with Christian mercy to forge a new path.</p> <p><i>Frostbound Hearts</i> is a gripping tale of love, courage, and transformation, where a shieldmaiden’s sword and a monk’s faith reshape a clan’s destiny. Perfect for fans of historical romance and epic sagas, this novel weaves rich Viking lore with a timeless story of defiance and hope.</p>"; 
